WEBVTT

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:06.270
I attempt to to find the missing component

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.200
which fragmented into fractions.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:18.280
I pursue the untouchable stars

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:24.750
till the end of the rainbow-colored sky.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:42.600
Trapped by the rays of light which always seem to find me,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.440
I mindlessly continued down this road.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.280
The accelerating gravitational force

00:00:50.360 --> 00:01:00.490
and the echoing dynamics are restraining my heart.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.330
Simply take me away.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.710
Take a glance through the ring

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:13.670
as the cosmic dust bridge is produced.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:17.140
Its form will alter at any given time

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:20.760
and cause our inception.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:25.390
Only to meet me once again.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.680
In this world, there's an infinite number of possible realities.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.560
This is one of them.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.400
It's a theoretical story that takes place in August.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.280
Looks like you've gotten used to this job, haven't you?

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.860
There's still a lot I don't remember, though.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.240
But I'll try my best.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:54.530
I know you will.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:55.410
All right!

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:59.080
Let's do our best, both at working and at getting your memory back!

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:00.290
Kent!

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:01.580
Pull yourself together!

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:02.540
Kent!

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:07.810
Kent!

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.630
Wake up!

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:11.650
Kent-san!

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.180
Don't go any closer.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.180
It's not something you should see.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.400
Shin...

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.140
Someone got him from behind.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:26.350
Whoever it was wanted him dead.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:27.730
His clothes are...

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.030
His belt got torn off!

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:33.170
Hey, Shin, does that mean...

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.410
Yeah. It is a message.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:38.450
Something important related to the criminal.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.250
How did it come to this?

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.000
You know, Ikki-san.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.420
I really don't think this is funny.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.220
If someone were to believe this and call the police,
it would create a lot of trouble for us.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.130
I should've figured that much.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:59.600
I always knew you were fit for being a detective.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.360
Kudos to you, Shin.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.990
I see. You're taking me for a fool.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.730
Oh, Kent.

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:07.110
You can get up now.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:11.820
So that's effort gone to waste, yes?

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:15.380
Seems like all the things I've done today have amounted to nothing.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.280
Huh? What's this?

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.260
Hidden camera?

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.880
U-Um...

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:23.660
What's wrong?

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:25.260
You look pale.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.790
Today was supposed to be "Meet a ghost" day, right?

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.710
You were scared, weren't you?

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.400
Could it be...

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.560
...that he's talking about <i>that</i>?

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.680
Good morning, everyone.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.760
As I presume you're aware,

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.270
recently a coffee shop opened
that has a concept similar to ours.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:50.160
Possibly influenced by that,
our shop has started to lose customers.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:56.910
I personally investigated the source of the rival shop's success without raising any suspicion.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:00.170
In order to avoid doing anything violent,

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:05.120
I've decided to set up a limited-time only fair here at this shop.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:10.750
So we will be hosting a different daily event for a week, right?

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:11.830
Yes.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:15.460
It's fine that it's up to us what each event is about,

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.630
but we're still pressed for time.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:21.470
About those daily events, it's all about how impactful they are, yes?

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:25.470
Well, it's not like we have to go all-out on them, right?

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:27.810
Looks like you're in for some hard times.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.640
Doesn't the fair start tomorrow?

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:34.270
Yes. We don't even know
what to do on the first day.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.400
If I remember correctly, tomorrow's event is...

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.510
Today you can enjoy darts in the shop.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.120
Try to get the highest score.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.010
Do your best.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.630
Welcome back, Master.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.800
Good day.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:00.630
The place's packed today.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:03.470
We're holding new events every day.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.230
Oh, so that's why there are people playing darts.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:08.310
Can I make an order?

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:09.830
A pastrami sandwich, please.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.700
And a brandy, right?

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.210
Yes, if it's not too much to ask.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.490
Right on target!

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.490
He's so cool!

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:29.410
He's too captivating.

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:31.290
He's drawing the customers' attention.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:34.170
They can't help it when he's like that.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:35.600
Based on that,

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:38.840
it seems like he has reconsidered tomorrow's plans.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.010
He's already done with the preparations.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.640
Here you can see the Summer Triangle.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:52.480
Its three brightest stars are:

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:53.980
Vega from the Lyra constellation,

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:53.980
Can I ask you something?

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.200
Deneb from the Cygnus constellation,

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:55.200
Yes.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.580
What constellation might that one there be?

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.580
and Altair from the Aquila constellation.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:59.000
Um...

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.320
Look, that one.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:02.030
No idea, huh?

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:04.590
Master, might I be of some use to you?

00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:07.200
I hope I can help you.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.500
No, never mind.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.500
Are you okay?

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:14.620
You know, you can't just go inside like that.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:15.790
I'm sorry.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.000
I...

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.500
You don't need to apologize.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.600
You didn't do anything bad.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.090
Sorry that I was late to follow you.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.170
It's okay.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:25.090
Thanks, Touma.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:27.260
If something happens, you can just come to me.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.930
I gotta say, though, it's kinda nostalgic.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:32.960
The starry sky.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:39.400
In the past, you, Shin, and I use to sneak out and gaze at the sky.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:43.500
You used to say "Amazing! Amazing!" while smiling cheerfully.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:45.950
It really brought me back.

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:48.010
<i>So something like that has happened.</i>

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:51.240
You know, that's not my job.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:54.500
Why did you decide to create an artificial starry sky?

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.580
Because of the mood it creates?

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:57.890
For the feelings it brings out.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:06:59.960
Now that we have it made,

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:03.130
why don't we move this conversation to the stars room?

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:05.170
I don't mind that,

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:08.760
but they don't really resemble the genuine stars, as they aren't accurate enough.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:12.600
There are stars that would be impossible to see with the naked eye.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.530
Excuse me, but please go back to work.

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:33.680
That was close.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:40.250
So you came all the way back here?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.840
Looks like we're out of black pepper.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:45.460
Do we have some stored?

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:46.470
Shin?

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:49.970
Kent-san, I'm taking a break.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:51.820
Go right ahead.

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:01.230
Come on, don't lick me.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:04.150
You're so cute!

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:07.490
What's this fluffiness?

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:09.200
You really are cute.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:14.950
We need to improve how we do things.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:17.580
The work suffers when we get distracted.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.750
Kent-san, it's because you
don't know how to handle animals.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.500
The animals shouldn't get in the way either, Shin.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:28.230
Now matter how much you train them,
they're still gonna do whatever they want.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:32.260
You should just try to be friendly with them.

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:34.610
Oh, right!

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:42.780
Sorry to keep you waiting, Miss.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:50.780
I'll entrust you with this.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:51.700
Okay.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:57.260
This is the thirty-seventh time...

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:02.800
Welcome back, Master.

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:05.960
You don't even look like maids and butlers now.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.840
Are you sure the shop is fine like this?

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:10.650
Not good.

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.590
Not good at all.

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:14.510
This doesn't make sense anymore.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:17.380
How much longer will we be wearing these?

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.640
The girls liked them, though.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:24.110
But, Ikki-san, some girls said they couldn't see your face in that costume.

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:26.150
That's not the problem here.

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:31.990
Considering that I, the cactus, and Shin, the rabbit,
bumped into each other over 157 times in that small kitchen,

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:34.650
we can't say this is working out.

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:37.040
This costume takes up a lot more space that you'd think.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.930
This goes deeper than that.

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:43.460
But the girls really seemed to be coping well.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:49.460
Hey, duck, your waddling was the cutest thing ever.

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:51.510
O-Oh, really?

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:53.320
You also look good.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:54.840
Thanks.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.180
It really makes me glad to hear that from you.

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:02.560
I guess this could work with more comfortable costumes.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.650
Comfortable?

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:08.210
Then what about this?

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:17.580
Welcome back, Misses.

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:24.640
Wearing glasses is a limited-time service.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.520
Thanks.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:33.840
Ikki's creativity knows no bounds.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:34.800
Um...

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.780
Are you all right, Kent-san?

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:38.650
Why do you ask?

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:42.140
Isn't it your first time serving customers?

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:43.930
Yet your glasses...

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:46.350
My eyesight is not altered that much.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:48.690
Well, I guess I could give it a try.

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:54.870
You did well on coming back, Sir.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:57.320
I want you to take the seat you like the most.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.820
Why is he talking like that?

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.300
K-Kent-san...

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:02.910
Was it a bit off?

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:06.370
Well then, Sir, let's have you change out of your coat now.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:07.960
Is it okay to change out of it?

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:13.630
Um, I think we should do it as Ikki-san does.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:15.420
As Ikki does?

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.760
I-I see.

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:19.600
It's not like my sight is that bad.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:23.690
I'm terribly sorry I couldn't distinguish your gender.

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:26.060
I deeply apologize, Miss.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:27.650
That's wrong!

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:28.270
Kent-san...

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:30.330
She didn't mean <i>that</i>.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:32.360
Well then, please come this way.

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:34.690
I hope you'll call for me when you have a request.

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:36.240
I'll serve you right away.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:38.740
Still speaking like that...

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:43.080
Kent, you were a total hoot!

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:47.250
Wasn't it you that told someone with no experience to try serving the customers?

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:49.960
I'm sorry you couldn't see much without glasses,

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:52.420
but it at least makes for a tense atmosphere, right?

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:55.130
Not like that's a good thing.

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:56.770
We weren't going for that, anyway.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:59.610
Maybe not, but the impact is important.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:04.620
If the costume is fine as is, then all we need to do is make the experience hard to forget?

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.020
Exactly.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:09.500
We need to mesmerize them.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:11.440
So...

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:13.650
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.300
Cry and scream!

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:29.120
You all are fated to come with me down to hell.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.120
That's as far as you go,

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.630
Demon Lord Kent!

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:38.720
Schutz Squad: Gentlemen!

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:41.440
Who are you?

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:45.480
Well, we're... the heroes of justice...

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:49.140
Shin, say it with confidence.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:51.230
Do you think I'm capable of that?

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:54.580
Your evil deeds will not be forgiven. Not today!

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:57.080
Bring it.

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:58.450
Let's go!

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:08.750
Everyone, we've destroyed the evil that lurked in this shop!

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:12.130
Call the Gentlemen whenever ill befalls you!

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:20.770
You didn't put much thought into
this cartoon costume event, did you?

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:24.350
You hated it as much as I expected, Shin.

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:26.760
That's why we didn't tell you until the last minute.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:29.140
It was hard work.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:31.810
Please don't say that with a smile on your face.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:34.100
Anyway, it just ruined the customers' mood.

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:36.040
Don't you think it was a failure?

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.280
Um...

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:39.990
So I saw your performance.

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:41.160
Ukyou-san?

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:46.910
You have no idea how to do a proper hero show.

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:48.200
We don't?

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:51.000
Ukyou-san, do you know a lot about them?

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:51.810
I do.

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:55.500
There were plenty of them when I started working.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.750
Anyway, just leave it to me.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.820
I'll make the best hero show you'll ever see.

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:08.570
Cry! Scream!

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:14.980
Every single one of you fools is destined to be brought down to hell with me!

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:19.730
Who dares laugh at me?

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:22.460
Do I look like a clown to you?

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:25.010
Fine, go ahead and laugh.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:31.040
I was the one who made this crappy act good,

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:33.970
and yet I get the role of the bad guy? Do they think I'm an idiot?

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:36.960
I'll show hell to all of you.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:40.210
I-If this goes on everyone will get killed!

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:44.090
Everyone, please call for the heroes of justice with all your strength.

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:45.110
Prepare, and...

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:47.610
Gentlemen!

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.270
Your days of evil end today!

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:55.110
Hey, you're up, Shin.

00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:57.650
Damn!

00:14:57.650 --> 00:15:00.110
"Be it as it may, I don't want to aim my weapon at you," Gentle Red.

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:03.570
"I'll protect you no matter what," Gentle Yellow.

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:08.620
"A mysterious girl is a charming girl," Gentle Blue.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:12.750
I don't like how they only teach you formulas in Math class.

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:14.460
I think Math is much more than that.

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:19.380
If we make it more entertaining, maybe people would—

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:19.380
And he's Gentle Green-san.

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:22.000
And the quartet is:

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.550
Schutz Squad: Gentlemen!

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:31.600
Hey, what was that explosion just now?

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:32.780
This'll kill us.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:34.060
Never mind that.

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:37.290
I know for a fact that something like this won't kill you.

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:38.290
Here I go.

00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:44.840
You never learn, huh?

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:46.780
You'll be fighting me now!

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:48.700
Take this!

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.370
Guys, let's use <i>that</i>.

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:56.620
Yeah. Let's end this here.

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:59.430
Certain death: Rainbow Exon!

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.730
Gentle Giga Fire!

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:09.220
We did it.

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:10.470
We defeated him.

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:11.470
Indeed.

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:14.140
This is a safe place now.

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:17.680
Everyone, call us if evil strikes back!

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:19.850
Evil can't be forgiven!

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:21.750
That's why we're called:

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:25.010
Schutz Squad: Gentlemen!

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:31.990
Oh? This was actually good?

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:34.450
They're liking it more than I expected.

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:36.750
I guess it's all thanks to Ukyou-san.

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:39.210
But isn't the steam lasting too long?

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:41.340
This is bad! If this doesn't stop...

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:53.510
I feel like reconsidering my life choices.

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:55.470
Do you really need to go that far?

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:59.140
Didn't you want to be part of a hero alliance when you were little?

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:00.940
Aren't you glad your dream has come true?

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:03.690
Are you kidding me? That was ages ago.

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:06.570
I won't do that embarrassing thing ever again.

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:08.460
Um, sorry.

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:13.030
It's all my fault for making you do things you shouldn't have, so it all went wrong.

00:17:13.030 --> 00:17:14.740
Besides...

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:19.600
I didn't think it through. It was just something that came to me.

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.590
I'm truly sorry!

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:25.000
The explosion and the fireworks were a problem, sure,

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:26.880
but you being too immersed in your villain role

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:29.180
and grabbing a customer was the real issue.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:33.930
We had to talk it out with him. It wasn't easy.

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:36.390
What's done's done.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:40.240
Ukyou-san helped us despite not working here.

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:45.060
Shouldn't the question be how will we learn from this experience?

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:47.370
It was quite a week, don't you think?

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:54.760
Thanks for working so hard, everyone.

00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:59.200
Th-Thanks.

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:01.460
Um, sorry...

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:03.600
You suffered because of me too.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:05.960
Don't worry. It didn't affect me.

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:10.300
We were the ones getting you involved in our problems.

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.860
The coffee today tastes different.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:19.940
It's a bit more bitter now.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:23.140
But I still like it, though.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:26.000
I didn't know they changed its flavor.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:28.320
The flavor of the coffee?

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:30.690
Kent, did you know that?

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:33.780
No, the bean is the same.

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:36.490
Maybe the way it's mixed changed.

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:37.760
Anyway,

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:45.640
isn't the concept of this shop to offer nice
coffee in a calm atmosphere to begin with?

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:49.440
I guess there are a lot of customers that come here to relax.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:54.260
But due to what we've been doing on this fair,

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:56.860
we may have scared those very same customers away.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:19:00.140
That reminds me, the other shop's traffic

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:04.330
declined soon after it opened.

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:07.440
They say the staff there

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:11.860
took the attracting customers business a bit too seriously and scared them away.

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:15.150
Now we know what <i>not</i> to do, right?

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:17.320
Is that what you're going with?

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:20.220
At any rate, overdoing it can't be good.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:21.700
Right?

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.920
We need to go back to who we were tomorrow.

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:26.600
Guess we'll clean this place up for now.

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:28.750
Can I leave you in charge?

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:31.480
Y-Yes, my pleasure.

00:19:32.590 --> 00:19:36.170
After all's done, they do get along, right?

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:37.360
Yes, they do.

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:40.610
When it counts, they're all in perfect harmony.

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:44.240
In this world, that's particularly powerful.

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.100
It's nothing.

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:49.270
Um...

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:51.370
I also think you're having fun with them.

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:55.490
I am. Although I'm making them help me.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:58.450
I'm glad you're doing okay.

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:03.200
This shop is a very important place for all of you, right?

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:05.120
I'm kind of jealous of that.

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:07.290
It's important for you too, isn't it, Ukyou-san?

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:13.270
When you come here, you seem—how do I put this—happy.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:16.090
You have this gentle look on your face.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:17.650
Well...

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:22.300
Whenever you don't show up, everyone here gets worried.

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:24.430
"I wonder what he's up to."

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:28.230
Ukyou-san, you're a very precious person for the people of this shop.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:32.160
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to—

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:37.290
No, you're right. This shop is a very important place for me as well.

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:46.290
I wouldn't mind if Shin and the others were kinder to me, though, considering that I am a regular customer.

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:48.310
You're right.

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:50.920
There's a nice air surrounding them.

00:20:50.920 --> 00:20:52.460
Is he a new rival?

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:54.310
Apparently so.

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:58.170
The hero show may have brought them closer together.

00:20:58.170 --> 00:21:01.260
It was also a mess because of him, though.

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:05.320
There you go, Ukyou-san. Here's your Habanero Pasta.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:08.180
I didn't order this.

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:10.890
You were helpful on the hero show.

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:13.230
It's our wish that you accept this as a token of our gratitude.

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:16.570
The advice you gave us was indeed good.

00:21:16.570 --> 00:21:19.590
We're sorry for how we treated you earlier.

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:21.740
Guys!

00:21:22.610 --> 00:21:24.160
Thank you!

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:31.750
By the way, Ikki, the sauce seems to be five times spicier than usual. Is that okay?

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:35.040
It's fine. I've tasted it.

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:36.460
I got a little teary, though.

00:21:36.460 --> 00:21:37.710
Okay, I wailed.

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:40.010
You're too immature.

00:21:40.010 --> 00:21:43.090
You even poured some Tabasco into it.

00:21:43.090 --> 00:21:45.180
So good!

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:47.990
Can I have some more Tabasco?

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:49.890
Is he serious?

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:51.860
Can't he notice it?

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:57.250
Especially when he sensed that subtle change of flavor in the coffee earlier.

00:21:58.360 --> 00:22:00.440
Ukyou-san is odd, huh?

00:22:00.440 --> 00:22:04.570
Hey, why are you all staring at me with that shocked looked on your faces?

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:08.410
He's a regular customer, so treat him nicely, okay?

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:10.410
And now you're being polite?

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:11.500
Why?

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:16.750
I finally got recognized as a regular, and even
thought I had made some new friends, and yet...

00:22:18.090 --> 00:22:21.760
It was a tough job, but it still ended up being fun, right?

00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:22.920
Yes.

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:26.100
And you got to know everyone a bit better, too.

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:31.930
I think talking about your memory loss with someone might be a good idea.

00:22:31.930 --> 00:22:33.890
Maybe.

00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:35.360
Those people...

00:22:36.520 --> 00:22:38.690
...are really childish.

00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:41.070
You seemed to be having fun too.

00:22:41.070 --> 00:22:42.360
Are you serious?

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:44.200
They're just manipulating fools.

00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:47.950
I'm the youngest of them all, so I get forced to do things.

00:22:49.660 --> 00:22:52.300
You're laughing a lot lately, aren't you?

00:22:53.580 --> 00:22:58.920
Until not long ago, you were an
apathetic girl with a loose screw.

00:23:00.300 --> 00:23:03.260
I can clearly notice that you've changed.

00:23:03.260 --> 00:23:04.680
Both Touma and I.

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:07.560
And I'd say Ikki and the rest, too.

00:23:09.050 --> 00:23:11.310
You thought we wouldn't notice?

00:23:11.310 --> 00:23:12.320
Don't be silly.

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.730
Shin, I...

00:23:14.730 --> 00:23:17.020
But you're all right, yeah?

00:23:17.020 --> 00:23:19.020
"I can't say it due to some circumstances,

00:23:19.020 --> 00:23:21.360
so I want to solve it somehow on my own."

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:25.070
I won't say a thing either, then.

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:28.110
You'll probably be uncomfortable if I try to force it out of you.

00:23:28.110 --> 00:23:30.200
You're oddly stubborn.

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:33.620
I'm sorry. I guess I'm making you worry.

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:36.080
I don't know what you're apologizing for, though.

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:39.170
All I'm saying is that you don't have to carry that burden by yourself.

00:23:39.840 --> 00:23:41.020
Shin.

00:23:41.250 --> 00:23:46.300
When you hit a wall, running around in circles won't solve anything.

00:23:47.090 --> 00:23:49.140
When things start to look bad, just talk to me.

00:23:49.140 --> 00:23:51.030
You don't need to be holding back after all these years.

00:23:52.390 --> 00:23:53.180
I know.

00:23:53.770 --> 00:23:56.400
Thank you, Shin.

00:24:02.020 --> 00:24:08.070
<i>I don't know where I can find my lost memories.</i>

00:24:08.950 --> 00:24:13.000
<i>But I'd like to do so and be able to remember everything.</i>

00:24:13.870 --> 00:24:18.370
<i>I hope they'll be able to help me when I'm at a loss,</i>

00:24:18.370 --> 00:24:23.170
<i>and that just like that, we can laugh together again, here.</i>

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:39.080
me no mae ni hirogaru hoshi no umi wo watatte iku

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:39.080
We sail across the ocean of stars that spreads out before us

00:24:39.240 --> 00:24:44.750
toritachi no kage sotto chijou miokuru

00:24:39.240 --> 00:24:44.750
We gently watch over the shadows of birds on the ground

00:24:45.250 --> 00:24:53.680
kirei na hako ni gyutto tsumekonda kinou made no omoi wo hakonde

00:24:45.250 --> 00:24:53.680
Carrying a pretty box stuffed with memories from days before

00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:57.680
dokomade tabi shiyou

00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:57.680
Let's travel the world

00:24:57.680 --> 00:25:03.310
sorezore ni chigau ikisaki wo kimete

00:24:57.680 --> 00:25:03.310
We each choose different destinations,

00:25:03.310 --> 00:25:10.730
awai kotoba mirai ni kaeru tame no kidou wo sagashiteru

00:25:03.310 --> 00:25:10.730
searching for the trajectory that will change faint words into our future

00:25:10.730 --> 00:25:16.870
kawaranai kokoro wo nigirishime

00:25:10.730 --> 00:25:16.870
Clutching that unchanging heart,

00:25:16.870 --> 00:25:22.950
memagurushii hibi wo kakenukete iku

00:25:16.870 --> 00:25:22.950
and running through dizzying days

00:25:22.950 --> 00:25:37.930
oboete iyouwo zuttosoushite natsukashii kioku ni naru made tobou

00:25:22.950 --> 00:25:37.930
Let's remember forever and fly until we become sweet memories
